 "item5_e3h4_diversity": {
  "label": "exploratory, post-freeze; descriptive only (card 4.3 item 7, E3-H4), no decision rule, no multiplicity correction",
  "definition": "cluster = prefix (both seeds together); B = 10,000, seed 5304 (default_rng([5304,0]) draws the prefix indices, the SAME in every arm; default_rng([5304,3]) the subsamples); percentile 95 percent intervals, reported raw (pct95_raw) and bias-centred (pct95_bias_centred = point + percentile - bootstrap mean; this is the one to quote, because duplicated prefixes in a resampled pool lower the rarefied entropy and distinct-2 of every replicate, so for a single arm the raw interval does not contain the point). Words = lower-cased completion text split on whitespace, as the frozen analysis. Unigram entropy = plug-in, nats, of exactly T_words = 2991 words drawn without replacement from the arm's pooled words (0.8 x the smallest arm total 3739; removes the sample-size bias; point = mean of 100 subsamples of the original pool, replicate = one subsample of the resampled pool; a replicate whose resampled pool is smaller than T is redrawn). Distinct-2 = distinct bigrams / T_bigrams = 2770 bigrams drawn without replacement (0.8 x the smallest arm total 3463); bigrams are formed WITHIN each completion, never across completions. Sibling noun Jaccard = mean over prefixes of |K0 & K1| / |K0 | K1| of the completion noun-key sets (frozen definition 4.3 item 7a; prefixes with both sets empty are skipped). E3-H4 direction: G lower diversity than P64 = Jaccard higher, entropy lower; a claim needs BOTH 95 percent intervals to exclude 0.",
  "caveats": [
   "bootstrap pools contain duplicated prefixes, so the without-replacement subsample entropy is slightly lower than at the point estimate (compare boot_mean with point); the raw interval is shifted accordingly and the bias-centred interval corrects the shift but is a normal-shift approximation, not BCa",
   "the frozen confirmatory.json diversity.distinct2 forms bigrams from a shuffled word subsample (np.random choice order), so it is not comparable with the distinct2 here and should not be quoted",
   "frozen entropy used T_ref = smallest arm total; point.unigram_entropy_nats_at_frozen_T_ref reproduces that definition (with this script's seed) for comparison"
  ],
